+// ---- Invocation coalescing (PS2X_INVOKE_COALESCE, default ON; =0 restores queue-everything).
+// PS2 INTC latches ONE status bit per cause: N vblanks while the handler cannot run deliver ONE
+// interrupt, not N (PCSX2 hwIntcIrq ORs I_STAT the same way), and sceGsSyncVCallback simply
+// misses vsyncs the EE slept through. Without this, a single long guest dispatch (>1s — e.g. a
+// host-pump chain with checkpoints suppressed) backlogs 60+ vblank deadlines which then fire in
+// ONE processDueDeadlines pass, each queueing a GsCallback/Interrupt invocation; the run loop
+// stacks them all before dispatching and the per-depth invocation stacks exhaust the 1MB async
+// arena at depth 64 ("EE invocation stack space exhausted"). Coalesce = drop an event-edge
+// invocation (GsCallback/Interrupt/Alarm) when an identical one (same kind + entry pc) is
+// already pending or stacked un-started; payload-carrying kinds are never coalesced.
+static const bool s_invokeCoalesce = []
+{ const char *e = std::getenv("PS2X_INVOKE_COALESCE"); return !(e && e[0] == '0'); }();
